      "notes": "Problems: Word export whose text layer drops most mathematics; transcribed from the page images. Page 3 of the problems file is a sponsors page (logos only) and is not transcribed. The printed paper gives no marks per question (\"The questions carry similar marks\"); the solutions for Qu 1 carry per-step marks [1]/[0.5] which are kept in the solution text; all points are null. The elliptical-orbit diagram on problems page 2 is a general aid for the whole paper; it is cropped once and attached to Qu 2 (p2-fig2, apogee/perigee) while the constants, orbit elements, Kepler's law and magnitude formula are in paper.documentNotes. Qu 5 prints \"Sir Arthur Edington\" in the introduction and \"Arthur Eddington\" in part a; the name is kept as printed in both places. Qu 5 part c prints lower-case $\\theta_s$ while part b uses $\\theta_S$; kept as printed. Solutions: Qu 1 (pages 1–3) interleaves the question text in blue italics, kept in italics. Qu 2 (pages 4–6) is a separate LaTeX document that restates the question with slightly different wording (e.g. \"a) Calculate how many days separate a supermoon.\", part f asks for the gravitational force instead of the field); its \"Supermoons\" introduction (Nolle 1979 / 90% definition), its lunar data list and its restated questions a)–f) are transcribed verbatim before the \"Solutions\" section (restored 2026-10-04; previously omitted). The underlined \"full moon\" in that restatement is kept as plain text. In its part f the printed formulas contain $\\mathrm{M}_{\\odot}$ (solar mass) where the Earth's mass is meant, and \"$G\\ \\mathrm{M}_{\\odot} M_{☽} + m$\" puts +m outside the Moon's mass; kept verbatim. Its part c prints $1.11^2 = 1.246$ (1.116² is meant); kept. The Moon symbol ☽ is written with \\text{☽}. Line-break hyphenations \"bright-est\" and \"super-moon\" are joined. Qu 3 solution (page 7) is a handwritten scan without a text layer, read at 300 dpi: the words were abbreviated and partly struck through (\"But [struck-out formula] we may write\"); the struck-out formula is omitted; \"147 AU\" and the digits of \"2.66\" in part d were overwritten in the handwriting but are legible. No official solutions exist for Qu 4 and Qu 5 (incomplete). Fix recorded: \"analagous\" → \"analogous\" (Qu 2 solution, page 6). Repaired 2026-10-04 from the independent verification (docs/verification/2026-10-0*-round*) of the agent:opus-5-5 (from-final) transcription.",
